  "body": "## What changed\n\n- New `crates/ui/src/egui_app/panes/table.rs`: the one command table. Each fixed command has one row with its id, label, ribbon group, menu and shortcut.\n- The ribbon reads its anchor groups (File, Setup, Modify, Inspect, View) from the table. `label_of` reads the label from the table. The tips read the shortcut hint from the table. The ribbon cells, labels, tips, icons and enabled rules do not change.\n- New `crates/ui/src/egui_app/panes/menu_bar.rs`: an in-app menu bar over the ribbon, with the menus File, Edit, Setup, Operation, Inspect and View.\n  - The Operation menu has one submenu for each catalog section that the machine can run, with each kind of that section. It also has Run.\n  - Each row shows the ribbon label, the shortcut hint and the ribbon enabled rule. A disabled row shows the reason on hover (`disabled_reason`; the Create rows keep their refusal tips).\n  - Each row runs `run_direct`, which calls the existing `crate::actions` layer. The menu adds no new state change. Model and Open go straight to their file dialogs, as the keys did before.\n- The keyboard layer (`panes::shortcuts`) reads its keys from the table. The keys and their modifier rules are the same as before.\n- Four commands that had only a key now have a `Cmd` and a menu row: Copy, Paste, Quit and Toggle projection. They are not on the ribbon.\n- `shell.rs`: one new top panel for the menu bar, before the ribbon panel (5 lines).\n- The menu titles have the AccessKit name \"<title> menu\" (\"View menu\"), and each menu row has its label as its name.\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/4484-command-table.md`.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew pinning tests in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/command_table.rs`:\n\n- `ribbon_and_menu_bar_list_the_same_command_ids` (each machine mode; with pins too)\n- `every_command_has_a_label_a_tip_and_an_enabled_rule`\n- `no_two_commands_share_a_shortcut` (also checks that each tip names its key)\n- `disabled_menu_rows_give_the_reason`\n- `file_menu_quit_runs_the_actions_layer`\n- `view_menu_projection_and_disabled_paste`\n- `operation_menu_creates_a_kind`\n- `layout_window_menu_bar` (the named layout test of the new bar, #1953)\n\nExisting tests that measure the window top now add the menu bar height:\n\n- `dropdown_icon_rows::op_dropdown_icon_and_label_follow_menu_metrics`, `dropdown_theme::all_dropdown_drawers_follow_theme_tokens`: the ribbon strip starts under the bar.\n- `structural::donate::layout_donate_top_right`, `update_check::title_bar_shows_update_notice_when_newer_release_is_injected_and_opens_notes_on_click`: the top band is under the bar.\n- `spindle_row::the_feeds_tab_offers_the_spindle_speed_and_its_unit_switch`: clicks `rpm` by AccessKit, because the row can now be under the fold at 720 px.\n- `page_layout_windows::layout_window_display_menu`: runs at 1366 x 768 (the plan's smallest screen, #4245). At 1280 x 720 the Display menu no longer fits above its button. Follow-up: #4491 (P7).\n\nThe ribbon structural and layout tests (`ribbon_accesskit`, `layout_shell`, the M6.2 ribbon tests) pass unchanged. `crates/ui` `#[test]` count: 2019 before, 2027 after. No snapshot PNG changes.\n\nReadings, head `3d7587869`, lane winbuild:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 11 steps, 0 failed (`ui lib` and 8 ui suites).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The quick gate was red on the two earlier heads (11 and then 2 position tests, listed above). I fixed them on this branch.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No change to toolpaths, posts or the project file, so no example catalog suite and no light lane step applies.\n- No native macOS menu bar (it needs a new dependency: maintainer decision).\n- No command search (P7 follow-up of #4245).\n- The Display menu at 1280 x 720 (follow-up #4491).\n- The menu was not tried by hand in the windowed app. The headless tests click it.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nAll at 1366 x 768, seeded document, dark theme.\n\nBefore (main):\n\n![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4490/before.png)\n\nAfter: the menu bar over the ribbon. The ribbon cells are the same.\n\n![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4490/after.png)\n\nAfter: the File menu open.\n\n![after-file-menu](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4490/after-file-menu.png)\n\nAfter: Operation > Milling 2D open. Dimmed kinds have no fitting tool, as on the ribbon.\n\n![after-operation-menu](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4490/after-operation-menu.png)\n\nChangelog: The app has a menu bar (File, Edit, Setup, Operation, Inspect, View) over the ribbon. The ribbon, the menu and the keyboard shortcuts read one command table.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #4484\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
